msgid "A harbour prices what you <0>give</0>. So a 2:1 harbour never applies to a commodity you give, but a resource you give keeps its 2:1 even when what you are buying is a commodity: 2 wood at a wood harbour buys 1 paper. There is no such thing as a paper harbour."
msgstr "A harbour prices what you <0>give</0>. So a 2:1 harbour never applies to a commodity you give, but a resource you give keeps its 2:1 even when what you are buying is a commodity: 2 wood at a wood harbour buys 1 paper. There is no such thing as a paper harbour."

